{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2119 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "53dd4bfa0febaf2959f4fede197dcc6b1f20ad90359dc9a83d8e83d81396f1e9" :edb/db-before-t 2118 :edb/db-after-t 2119 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535431 50 #inst "2026-10-08T23:56:32.692Z" 13194139535431 true] [17592186147368 1020 #edb/ref 17592186348753 13194139535431 true] [17592186147368 1020 #edb/ref 17592186348760 13194139535431 true] [17592186348753 1017 #edb/ref 17592186348754 13194139535431 true] [17592186348753 1089 "q-129258" 13194139535431 true] [17592186348753 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535431 true] [17592186348753 1100 "Given the two planes $x-5y+2z=0$ and $3x-2y+7=0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The normal vectors of the planes are parallel.\n- The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $0.$\n- The planes intersect on a line." 13194139535431 true] [17592186348753 1113 #uuid "32658552-b15a-5af7-93c5-13bdae918ffc" 13194139535431 true] [17592186348753 1145 "First, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $x-5y+2z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨1,-5,2⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $3x-2y+7=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨3,-2,0⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statements I and II are false. Indeed, computing the cross product of the normal vectors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨1,-5,2⟩\\times ⟨3,-2,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =4i+6j+13k \\\\  & =⟨4,6,13⟩\\ne 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}\\ne 0$, the vectors ${n}_{1}$ and ${n}_{2}$ are not parallel.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, two non-parallel planes in $3$-dimensional space must intersect on a line.\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true." 13194139535431 true] [17592186348754 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348755 13194139535431 true] [17592186348754 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348756 13194139535431 true] [17592186348754 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348757 13194139535431 true] [17592186348754 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348758 13194139535431 true] [17592186348754 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348759 13194139535431 true] [17592186348754 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535431 true] [17592186348754 1041 "selection" 13194139535431 true] [17592186348754 1104 #edb/ref 17592186348758 13194139535431 true] [17592186348754 1110 #uuid "aecc0f8f-d563-5c1d-b722-ee5aeb098b76" 13194139535431 true] [17592186348755 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535431 true] [17592186348755 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535431 true] [17592186348755 1111 #uuid "7c6d4629-4b4d-58b2-84f4-efc7a0475cf6" 13194139535431 true] [17592186348756 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535431 true] [17592186348756 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535431 true] [17592186348756 1111 #uuid "d2a591bc-546a-53a8-95a1-149c1c96f456" 13194139535431 true] [17592186348757 1034 "I only" 13194139535431 true] [17592186348757 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535431 true] [17592186348757 1111 #uuid "ac1d458d-ad7f-5879-9492-422252cdc8ce" 13194139535431 true] [17592186348758 1034 "III only" 13194139535431 true] [17592186348758 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535431 true] [17592186348758 1111 #uuid "49af3ebc-841a-58b3-89ed-84c600117d34" 13194139535431 true] [17592186348759 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535431 true] [17592186348759 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535431 true] [17592186348759 1111 #uuid "14194db7-0721-550f-a526-89686b6a0c07" 13194139535431 true] [17592186348760 1017 #edb/ref 17592186348761 13194139535431 true] [17592186348760 1089 "q-129260" 13194139535431 true] [17592186348760 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535431 true] [17592186348760 1100 "Given the two planes $3x+y-2z=0$ and $2x+y+3z+7=0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $⟨5,-13,1⟩.$\n- The planes are parallel.\n- The planes intersect on a line." 13194139535431 true] [17592186348760 1113 #uuid "733437c7-f788-5c6d-8f50-510c19df1880" 13194139535431 true] [17592186348760 1145 "First, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $3x+y-2z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨3,1,-2⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $2x+y+3z+7=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨2,1,3⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Computing the cross product of the normal vectors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨3,1,-2⟩\\times ⟨2,1,3⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =5i-13j+k \\\\  & =⟨5,-13,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}\\ne 0$, the vectors ${n}_{1}$ and ${n}_{2}$ are not parallel. As a result, the corresponding planes are not parallel either.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, two non-parallel planes in $3$-dimensional space must intersect on a line.\n\nTherefore, only I and III only are true." 13194139535431 true] [17592186348761 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348762 13194139535431 true] [17592186348761 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348763 13194139535431 true] [17592186348761 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348764 13194139535431 true] [17592186348761 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348765 13194139535431 true] [17592186348761 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348766 13194139535431 true] [17592186348761 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535431 true] [17592186348761 1041 "selection" 13194139535431 true] [17592186348761 1104 #edb/ref 17592186348763 13194139535431 true] [17592186348761 1110 #uuid "5ca36a7a-1ef0-5011-ad6e-eb40f3682405" 13194139535431 true] [17592186348762 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535431 true] [17592186348762 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535431 true] [17592186348762 1111 #uuid "6b5fd7a3-28be-588a-9f00-9c215cf4ceb6" 13194139535431 true] [17592186348763 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535431 true] [17592186348763 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535431 true] [17592186348763 1111 #uuid "006f54c9-8c2e-5697-88bf-61388ef3b305" 13194139535431 true] [17592186348764 1034 "